{"title":"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Only_Simple_Concepts,_w/_Video)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Only Simple Concepts, w/ Video)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a cyclic quadrilateral satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47ea9c53c9595185853839968992bb803d1dc8a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD^2 + BC^2 = AB^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"154\" height=\"16\" />. The diagonals of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87fb4607141ba7f24ba18ac4c821b669d2d644b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APD = \\angle BPC$\" width=\"136\" height=\"13\" />. Show that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0edebe902653b343eee6f0a6a93a09f80884504e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d9f6cc8ede9cff2d437369fc69461a87aab80b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PE \\cap DC = M$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" />. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\nNote that only one point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> satisfies the given angle condition. With this in mind, construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with the following properties:\n</p><p>(1) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca75578791b1b0c3a4dde59d6984bcd2c29084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP&#39; \\cdot AB = AD^2$\" width=\"133\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>(2) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dab35b7c77f27cf5f73a526b822f576183ee5c6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP&#39; \\cdot AB = CD^2$\" width=\"135\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Claim: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82bf9d9aabe5a4391998eef8b4702df2519a1f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = P&#39;$\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Proof:\nThe conditions imply the similarities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7f11c8ef1f523893cd076b1577a00920548938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADP \\sim ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1abf0f4b29bafdcf9fdaa4fb012bb049b450bb96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCP \\sim BAC$\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" /> whence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e77ac0759fe6fcd226ff9bc7ef5cc9f62a8bd9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle APD = \\measuredangle BDA = \\measuredangle BCA = \\measuredangle CPB$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"296\" height=\"13\" /> as desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Claim: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0edebe902653b343eee6f0a6a93a09f80884504e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is a symmedian in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ece55f9a0c8c69d74514764c04b2a52b1cf734e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Proof:\nWe have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1526ef8dba532a79bd26467743ed5d3f0ec09545.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  AP \\cdot AB = AD^2 \\iff AB^2 \\cdot AP &amp;= AD^2 \\cdot AB \\\\ \\iff \\left( \\frac{AB}{AD} \\right)^2 &amp;= \\frac{AB}{AP} \\\\ \\iff \\left( \\frac{AB}{AD} \\right)^2 - 1 &amp;= \\frac{AB}{AP} - 1 \\\\ \\iff \\frac{AB^2 - AD^2}{AD^2} &amp;= \\frac{BP}{AP} \\\\ \\iff \\left(\\frac{BC}{AD} \\right)^2 &amp;= \\left(\\frac{BE}{AE} \\right)^2 = \\frac{BP}{AP}  \\end{align*}\" width=\"406\" height=\"224\" />\nas desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the isogonal conjugate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c0c38ce2e21c2cbedc371b362c91343c2dbfee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle PEA = \\measuredangle MEC = \\measuredangle BEN$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"223\" height=\"13\" />. However <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a4af46823c614b0cdf5876025d7931df4bb084c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle MEC = \\measuredangle BEN$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"144\" height=\"13\" /> implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> from similar triangles, so we are done. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2019_USAMO_2.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/2019_USAMO_2.png/450px-2019_USAMO_2.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"430\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/58/2019_USAMO_2.png 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2019_USAMO_2a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ad/2019_USAMO_2a.png/450px-2019_USAMO_2a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"345\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ad/2019_USAMO_2a.png/675px-2019_USAMO_2a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ad/2019_USAMO_2a.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f386fc0035258fe8780a97b973f9ea93679abf16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> be the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f6f7cd16a47f33bebcf3fc361eeb808b630504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC.$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>We denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d3ba7373610c94bd24a19688f322822e4cbfff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3ded91c12b02abcd11cbb8f256ff8eddb7619b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_\\Omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> inversion with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/85955932018c71ba9f22e9b97cafda1c5da07b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b97cd6877fa8dbd8fc7381b6c1c1a9930a781d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B&#39;= I_\\omega (B), C&#39;= I_\\omega (C), D = I_\\omega (D) \\implies\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f90cbd28cd1c86d66600521d0b714bc00ed523.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB&#39; \\cdot AB = AD^2,  \\angle ACB = \\angle AB&#39;C&#39;.\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/4/614a687005a8ce2fdd3e5f7dd94efb99e5a128ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A&#39;= I_\\Omega (A), D&#39;= I_\\Omega (D), C = I_\\Omega (C) \\implies\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/028012df27a02be6e31fa99ea544dea4dac1e9f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BA&#39; \\cdot AB = BC^2,  \\angle BDA = \\angle BA&#39;D&#39;.\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"19\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae54b43c219341de4a6e5919922cf55371e6ee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e205508a68627033b7ad6a521e02aa48ece7378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_\\omega (\\theta) = B&#39;C&#39;D,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" /> straight line, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b7799f1317e3b85863b7d4cc232f2b807ef905.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AB&#39;C&#39; = \\angle AB&#39;D&#39; = \\angle ACB.\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"14\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4dd3e03b47215708f576f09ab3d7b150330a6fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_\\Omega (\\theta) = A&#39;D&#39;C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> straight line, therefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee9dd40fd227512bef60f73e0566a649168ad04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BA&#39;D&#39; = \\angle BA&#39;C = \\angle BDA.\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/6/ef6b8b313cb26dcbf80b3eb24eb7a75246cc9b3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle BA&#39;C = \\angle AB&#39;D.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"197\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0abe9458b1546e6d557c8efe7d28af828bf794db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB&#39; + BA&#39; = \\frac {AD^2 + BC^2 }{AB} = AB \\implies\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"39\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are coincide.\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46bb6cd775175383f6d0a606097d34842f45d462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39; = B&#39; = Q \\in AB.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Suppose, we move point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95fbfb49b675ba11392ba7c2603d0c87f89be76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/803ec09f67c9ef4e1f22e158615e6c64771e1b13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AQD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> decreases monotonically, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b262ed0bfdf2f74c19e2e7b0ff2798dd889fec8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BQC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> increases monotonically. So, there is only one point where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b959fcf644ae75791692431f2b2a91479d9d16fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AQD = \\angle BQC \\implies P = Q.\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/857bc63de65d9f7ab6a67d2dd8c33ce7a3eacb9d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B = I_\\omega (P), D&#39; = I_\\omega (D&#39;), C&#39; = I_\\omega (C), A = I_\\omega (\\infty) \\implies\\]\" width=\"420\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2c6cad6b90abb0406127b6d3670dbdaff8d56e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hspace{19mm} I_\\omega (CD&#39;P) = AC&#39;D&#39;B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"264\" height=\"20\" /> is cyclic.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dc4da1c632d89de12499189941ac82b13ec23c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle ACD = \\angle ABD = \\angle CC&#39;D \\implies C&#39; D&#39; || CD \\implies\\]\" width=\"390\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/537789a9e52564703b3569c3e68115ea52234696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hspace{19mm} C&#39;D&#39;CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"161\" height=\"16\" /> is  trapezoid.\n</p><p>It is known that the intersection of the diagonals, intersection point of the lines containing the lateral sides of the trapezoid and the midpoints of two parallel sides are collinear.\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Only_Simple_Concepts.2C_w.2F_Video.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Only_Simple_Concepts,_w/_Video)\">Solution 3 (Only Simple Concepts, w/ Video)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Only Simple Concepts, w/ Video)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Video: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rbnW3iBr7rU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rbnW3iBr7rU</a>\n</p><p>This solution is divided into two parts: proving that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a66206dedaef978be2e53d554484b8a0b58fcf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, and proving that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear.\n</p><p><b>Part 1</b>\n</p><p>Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> the circle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> the circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> the circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a971b41c17969c79e902bc1004bb2b66e7eee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\neq C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> the intersection between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/1456e69d3433893faf917e69be7af561ae27b7b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T \\neq D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> the intersection between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>The two points of intersection between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> are symmetric about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, and if we let one of them be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, we have that\n\\begin{align*}\nAX^2 + BX^2 = AD^2 + BC^2 = AB^2\n\\end{align*}\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f24abe7d0f9fe18965a561fb63a317096b8f583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AXB = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"34\" /> by Pythagorean's Theorem and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. In other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> concur on the two symmetric points and the three circle's radical axes are all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> the intersection between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/6/c46732cc54ebf7b9abd5412d340937bc62972493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/6/c46732cc54ebf7b9abd5412d340937bc62972493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is the radical axis of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> has equal powers to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, and hence all four circles. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is the radical center of the four circles and hence it also lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d9f1ff4706cf9340a5a24d275fafb46157c9b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, the radical axis of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>To prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a66206dedaef978be2e53d554484b8a0b58fcf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />'s angle condition makes it unique on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, it suffices to show that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\angle AQD = \\angle BQC \\\\\\\\\n\\Longleftrightarrow \\angle QAD + \\angle QDA = \\angle QBC + \\angle QCB \\\\\\\\\n\\Longleftrightarrow \\angle BAD + \\angle ADT = \\angle ABC + \\angle BCS \\\\\\\\\n\\Longleftrightarrow \\angle BAD + \\angle ABD = \\angle ABC + \\angle BAC \\\\\\\\\n\\Longleftrightarrow \\angle ADB = \\angle ACB\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p><b>Part 2</b>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e88659988ba5f56800d97832acb4d3c3fecb628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K = DT \\cap AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717cbc64b2cbf170caf46767e93558b98f0537e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L = CS \\cap DB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"115\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a975d0b3c834f22853424759cb7798500d80f254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M&#39; = QE \\cap DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"19\" />. By Ceva's theorem on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75b83c9b1c658d2188ab619d0e212fa73ced1f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QDC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />,\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{CM'}{M'D} * \\frac{DK}{KQ} * \\frac{QL}{LC} = 1\n\\end{align*}\nSince we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/7857325dd647a3cae4875068f03843b26cf50710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M&#39; = M$\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />, which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13d185518d87337bb4634ab4c2001ebc8f5659d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CM&#39;}{M&#39;D} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"40\" />. It suffices to show\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{DK}{KQ} =  \\frac{CL}{LQ}\n\\end{align*}\nIt is well known by Law of Sines on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/2454492dc726a0ba8873201d86b53994f2e65659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c27703e0d7603c1407eee5fc8e573b60cd95f14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BQC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{DK}{KQ} = \\frac{\\sin \\angle DAK}{\\sin \\angle KAQ} * \\frac{AD}{AQ} \\\\\\\\\n\\frac{CL}{LQ} = \\frac{\\sin \\angle CBL}{\\sin \\angle LBQ} * \\frac{BC}{BQ}\n\\end{align*}\nEquating the two expressions, we now want to show that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\sin \\angle DAK}{\\sin \\angle KAQ} * \\frac{AD}{AQ} = \\frac{\\sin \\angle CBL}{\\sin \\angle LBQ} * \\frac{BC}{BQ} \\\\\\\\\n\\Longleftrightarrow \\frac{AD}{AQ * BC} = \\frac{BC}{BQ * AD} \\\\\\\\\n\\Longleftrightarrow \\frac{AQ}{AD^2} = \\frac{BQ}{BC^2} \\\\\\\\\n\\Longleftrightarrow \\frac{AQ}{AX^2} = \\frac{BQ}{BX^2}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>We are now looking at the right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d5c1dd8c6a912fb68b13960be19827f3d07462a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XBQA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, in which we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536365a5d9986d33a8dfc5bf749d36d1c817a426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XBA = \\angle ABQ = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />. Then, the expression simplifies to\n\\begin{align*}\n\\Longleftrightarrow \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{AX} = \\frac{cos \\theta}{BX} \\\\\\\\\n\\Longleftrightarrow \\tan \\theta = \\frac{AX}{BX}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>QED.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO\" title=\"2019 USAMO\">2019 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018011504\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.061 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.084 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 676/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22563/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.682      1 -total\n 55.55%    8.156      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 42.46%    6.234      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17479:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018011504 and revision id 274911. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}